              "type": "output_text",
              "annotations": [],
              "logprobs": [],
              "text": "{\"answerText\":\"**No—an as-of-right determination for a specific property cannot be made from the supplied facts.** The property’s address or BBL and controlling mapped zoning-district/Appendix J status are necessary to determine which allowance applies; no map location can be inferred here.\\n\\nIn Manufacturing Districts, a self-service storage facility is marked “♦P” in every M1, M2, and M3 column: “♦” means permitted with limitations and “P” denotes additional conditions. (ZR § 42-191.) Section 42-192 applies to ♦ uses. In an Appendix J Subarea 1 designated area, storage is subject to the stated as-of-right provisions, including the limitation to establishments providing industrial floor space or the specified “business-sized” storage space. In Subarea 2, it instead requires a City Planning Commission special permit under ZR § 74-192. (ZR § 42-192; Appendix J; ZR § 74-192.) Appendix J identifies designated-area maps and distinguishes Subareas 1 and 2, but the supplied text does not locate this property on a map.\\n\\nThe December 19, 2017 rule is a separate existing-facility path: a facility that existed on that date in a designated area may be conforming if satisfactory DOB documentation was filed; enlargements/extensions have the stated relief only if there is no increase in the zoning lot’s area as it existed on that date. That path cannot be applied without the facility’s dated existence, DOB filing/documentation status, and historical/current zoning-lot-area facts. (ZR § 42-192.) The “P” notation also makes the supplied performance-standard provisions applicable to this use. (ZR § 42-193.)\",\"supportedPoints\":[{\"heading\":\"Manufacturing-district table classification\",\"explanation\":\"The ZR § 42-191 table classifies a self-service storage facility as Use Group IX(A), use D2, and shows “♦P” in each M1, M2, and M3 column. The passage defines “♦” as permitted with limitations and “P” as additional conditions.\",\"sectionID\":\"20022472\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"37719109-7c96-41cd-9e71-bc3c3f4b99b3\"]},{\"heading\":\"Appendix J determines the designated-area path\",\"explanation\":\"For ♦ uses, ZR § 42-192 applies. It provides that Appendix J Subarea 1 designated areas are subject to the stated as-of-right provisions, including industrial floor space or specified business-sized storage; Subarea 2 requires a City Planning Commission special permit pursuant to ZR § 74-192. Appendix J distinguishes Subarea 1 maps from Subarea 2 maps for those respective paths. The supplied evidence does not establish this property's mapped location.\",\"sectionID\":\"20022473\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"a03e78e1-4194-40f5-bab7-f300f36ab2a7\"]},{\"heading\":\"Appendix J map categories\",\"explanation\":\"Appendix J states that boundaries of designated areas within Manufacturing Districts are shown on its maps, with Subarea 1 for the as-of-right provisions of ZR § 42-19 and Subarea 2 for the City Planning Commission special-permit path under ZR § 74-192. The listed area names and map numbers do not establish whether an unidentified property lies within any mapped boundary.\",\"sectionID\":\"20021237\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"3e6faec1-356b-4174-9e1b-32bd81ed0b42\"]},{\"heading\":\"Subarea 2 special-permit route\",\"explanation\":\"ZR § 74-192 authorizes the City Planning Commission to permit a self-service storage facility on zoning lots in Appendix J Subarea 2 designated areas, subject to the Commission's finding that the zoning lot is appropriate based on the land-use characteristics of the lot and surrounding area. This is not an as-of-right route.\",\"sectionID\":\"20019206\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"94f40cba-660b-46cc-b2eb-be5a20673867\"]},{\"heading\":\"Existing-facility provisions and additional conditions\",\"explanation\":\"ZR § 42-192 provides a separate treatment for a self-service storage facility that existed on December 19, 2017, in an Appendix J designated area: it may be conforming if satisfactory documentation was filed with DOB showing both its existence on that date and compliance with the supplied self-service-storage definition reference. The stated enlargement/extension relief applies only where there is no increase in zoning-lot area from that existing on December 19, 2017. Separately, because the table marks the use “P,” ZR § 42-193 applies its performance-standard requirement to the use, except for the enumerated unrelated uses.\",\"sectionID\":\"20022473\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"a03e78e1-4194-40f5-bab7-f300f36ab2a7\"]},{\"heading\":\"P-marked use performance standards\",\"explanation\":\"ZR § 42-193 states that, except for boat storage, public parking garages, and public parking lots, all uses denoted “P” in ZR § 42-191 must conform to the performance standards in ZR §§ 42-40 through 42-48, inclusive. Self-service storage is marked “♦P” in the supplied table.\",\"sectionID\":\"20022474\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"54eafd1e-6ff6-49e7-a53a-c633dc89708e\",\"37719109-7c96-41cd-9e71-bc3c3f4b99b3\"]}],\"assumptions\":[],\"missingFacts\":[\"Property address or BBL, and the controlling official zoning-map or verified mapped-district evidence needed to identify the applicable zoning district and Appendix J map location.\",\"Whether the property is within a special district or subject to special-district controls that materially affect the requested use determination.\",\"Whether the property is within an Appendix J designated area and, if so, whether it is mapped in Subarea 1 or Subarea 2.\",\"For a potential December 19, 2017 existing-facility path: whether a qualifying self-service storage facility existed on that date, whether satisfactory documentation was filed with DOB, and whether it met the referenced definition on that date.\",\"Current zoning-lot area and, if relying on the existing-facility enlargement/extension provision, the zoning-lot area as it existed on December 19, 2017.\",\"If Subarea 1 applies, whether the proposed facility provides industrial floor space or the specified business-sized storage space.\",\"Performance-standard compliance inputs under ZR §§ 42-40 through 42-48, because the proposed use is P-marked; the supplied evidence does not provide their technical criteria.\"],\"followUpQuestions\":[],\"evidenceLimitations\":[\"This answer is limited to the supplied continuously amended NYC Zoning Resolution text through August 13, 2026. The supplied ZR § 42-192 excerpt omits detailed Subarea 1 industrial/business-sized-space, signage, and reporting provisions, and the supplied Appendix J text identifies map categories but does not provide a selected map or establish any property's mapped location.\",\"The supplied ZR § 74-192 passage is truncated after part of the Commission's listed considerations; it supports only the special-permit route and stated appropriateness finding described above, not a complete special-permit analysis.\"],\"additionalEvidenceNeeded\":[\"A property-specific zoning analysis using the address or BBL and the controlling official zoning map and applicable Appendix J map.\",\"Applicable special-district mapping and enacted special-district text, if the property is mapped in a special district.\",\"For an existing-facility claim, DOB-acceptable documentation of the December 19, 2017 facility, its qualifying status, relevant DOB filing status, and historical zoning-lot area records.\",\"If a Subarea 1 as-of-right proposal is pursued, the complete applicable ZR § 42-192 provisions and proposal information sufficient to evaluate the industrial-floor-space or business-sized-storage condition.\"] ,\"supportingSourceUses\":[],\"citations\":[{\"sectionID\":\"20022472\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"37719109-7c96-41cd-9e71-bc3c3f4b99b3\"],\"relevance\":\"Classifies self-service storage as ♦P in M1, M2, and M3 and defines the table notations.\"},{\"sectionID\":\"20022473\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"a03e78e1-4194-40f5-bab7-f300f36ab2a7\"],\"relevance\":\"Establishes Appendix J Subarea 1 and Subarea 2 paths and the December 19, 2017 existing-facility provisions.\"},{\"sectionID\":\"20022474\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"54eafd1e-6ff6-49e7-a53a-c633dc89708e\"],\"relevance\":\"Establishes performance-standard applicability for P-marked uses.\"},{\"sectionID\":\"20019206\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"94f40cba-660b-46cc-b2eb-be5a20673867\"],\"relevance\":\"Establishes the City Planning Commission special-permit route for Appendix J Subarea 2.\"},{\"sectionID\":\"20021237\",\"sourceIDs\":[\"3e6faec1-356b-4174-9e1b-32bd81ed0b42\"],\"relevance\":\"Identifies Appendix J's designated-area mapping and Subarea 1/Subarea 2 distinction.\"}]}"
